<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kościuszko Uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1794">1794</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kosciuszko Uprising was a revolt led by Tadeusz Kosciuszko in 1794 against Russian and Prussian domination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> following the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-partition-of-poland">Second Partition</a>. Despite early successes, it was crushed by Russian and Prussian forces. Its defeat led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-partition-of-poland">Third Partition</a> of 1795, which ended the Commonwealth's existence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kosciuszko-uprising.jpg" alt="Kościuszko Uprising" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BorysMapping · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ko%C5%9Bciuszko_uprising.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…of 1792 and the Targowica Confederation; the Second Partition of 1793 stripped away further vast territories; and the <b>Kościuszko Uprising</b> of 1794, an attempt to mobilise the whole nation including the peasantry, was crushed by Russian and Prussian forces, leading directly to the Third Partition of 1795, which…</blockquote><a href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1796 Józef Wybicki, a leading moderate émigré politician, proposed Polish Legions within the French Revolutionary Army and persuaded General Jan Henryk Dąbrowski, a hero of the 1794 <b>Kościuszko Uprising</b>, to put the plan to the French Directory.</blockquote><a href="/songs/poland-is-not-yet-lost">Poland Is Not Yet Lost</a></li><li><blockquote>His speech is considered the start of the <b>Kościuszko Uprising</b>, whose defeat led to the Third Partition of 1795.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/march-24">24 March in history</a></li></ul></section>
